# retroforge built-in firmware list (CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE) — the union of blobs baked
# into Image.gz so they are present before the rootfs mounts. One /lib/firmware-relative
# path per line; kernel/build.sh resolves each against firmware/linux-fw/ (open blobs,
# fetch-linux-fw.sh) then firmware/qcom-fw/ (device blobs, fetch-qcom-fw.sh) and derives
# CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE from this list. Add a SoC/board by appending its early-boot blobs
# here — no edit to build.sh. Comments (#) and blank lines ignored.
#
# No AudioReach topologies, DSP images or amp ACF blobs: nothing asks for them before the root
# mounts. q6apm (SND_SOC_QDSP6_APM=m) requests qcom/<card driver>/<card model>-tplg.bin once the
# ADSP is up, and the ADSP boots from the QCOM_Q6V5_PAS module on the root, so the copies in the
# root's /lib/firmware load; built in, they only lengthened Image.gz. The names follow the card:
# the Thor's AYN-Thor is a byte-identical copy of AYN-Odin2's, and the SM4450 boards' card driver
# reports sm8450.

# --- sm8750: Adreno 830 GPU microcode + zap shader (open, linux-firmware) — shared by
# both SM8750 boards (AYN Odin 3, KONKR Pocket FIT Elite); embedded for the usual reason:
# DRM_MSM is =y and the panel is the only console, so the GPU inits before the root mounts.
qcom/gen80000_aqe.fw
qcom/gen80000_sqe.fw
qcom/gen80000_gmu.bin
qcom/sm8750/gen80000_zap.mbn

# --- sm8650: Adreno 750 GPU microcode (open, linux-firmware) ---
qcom/gen70900_aqe.fw
qcom/gen70900_sqe.fw
qcom/gmu_gen70900.bin

# --- sm8650: GPU zap shader (open, linux-firmware) — shared across all boards ---
qcom/sm8650/gen70900_zap.mbn

# --- sm8550: Adreno 740 GPU microcode + zap shader (open, linux-firmware) ---
# All three ship in linux-firmware (a740_zap under the qcom/sm8550/ subdir); embedded so
# the GPU can init before the rootfs mounts. Shared across every SM8550 board.
qcom/a740_sqe.fw
qcom/gmu_gen70200.bin
qcom/sm8550/a740_zap.mbn

# --- sm8250: Adreno 650 GPU microcode + zap shader (open, linux-firmware) ---
# Shared by all six SM8250 boards. Embedded for the same reason as the other two SoCs:
# DRM_MSM is =y and the panel is the only console, so the GPU has to come up before the
# root is mounted.
qcom/a650_sqe.fw
qcom/a650_gmu.bin
qcom/sm8250/a650_zap.mbn

# --- sm6115: Adreno 610 GPU microcode ---
# The A610 runs the A630 SQE firmware (open, linux-firmware) and has no GMU. Its zap shader is NOT
# here: msm-firmware-loader serves the device's own from its vendor partition, and built-in
# firmware is searched first, so an embedded copy would shadow it. msm inits the GPU on first
# open and retries on the next one if that fails, so nothing needs the zap before the root mounts.
qcom/a630_sqe.fw

# --- sm4450: Adreno 613 zap shader ---
# The A613 runs the A630 SQE firmware, already listed for the SM6115 above, and has no GMU. Its
# zap shader (shared by both boards' DTS) comes from the qcom-firmwares repo
# (firmware/QCOM_FW.pin); embedded for the same reason as the other SoCs.
qcom/sm4450/a613_zap.mbn
